What does this log?

```js
const b = Buffer.from([0xfb, 0xff]);
console.log(b.toString('base64'), b.toString('base64url'));
```

This export job ignores the return value of `write()`:

```js
const out = fs.createWriteStream('export.csv');
for (const row of millionRows) out.write(toCsv(row));
out.end();
```

The file is eventually complete and correct, but memory peaks at several GB. Why?

What is written to `out` here?

```js
const { pipeline } = require('node:stream/promises');
const seen = [];
await pipeline(
  Readable.from(['a', 'b']),
  async function* (source) {
    for await (const chunk of source) yield chunk.toUpperCase();
  },
  new Writable({ objectMode: true, write(c, e, cb) { seen.push(c); cb(); } }),
);
console.log(seen.join(''));
```

A cache stores 10-byte keys cut from large incoming buffers:

```js
socket.on('data', (chunk) => {     // chunks of about 64 KiB
  cache.set(chunk.subarray(0, 10), Date.now());
});
```

Memory grows far faster than 10 bytes per key. Why?

What does this log?

```js
const p = new PassThrough();
p.write('ab');
p.write('cd');
p.once('readable', () => {
  const chunks = [];
  let c;
  while ((c = p.read()) !== null) chunks.push(c.toString());
  console.log(chunks);
});
```

This Transform never calls its callback:

```js
const t = new Transform({
  objectMode: true,
  transform(chunk, enc, cb) { this.push(chunk); },
});
Readable.from([1, 2, 3]).pipe(t).on('data', console.log);
```

Which two statements describe what happens? (Choose two.)

How many chunks does this loop see?

```js
const chunks = [];
for await (const c of Readable.from('abc')) chunks.push(c);
console.log(chunks.length, chunks[0]);
```

What does this log?

```js
const r = Readable.from([1, 2, 3, 4]);
for await (const x of r) {
  if (x === 2) break;
}
console.log(r.destroyed);
```

An HTTP handler awaits a slow auth check before it starts reading the request body:

```js
async function handler(req, res) {
  await checkAuth(req.headers.authorization); // 300 ms
  let body = '';
  for await (const chunk of req) body += chunk;
  // ...
}
```

The client finished sending the body within 50 ms. What happens to it?

Assume a Writable whose `_write` completes asynchronously. What does this log?

```js
const w = new Writable({
  objectMode: true,
  highWaterMark: 3,
  write(chunk, enc, cb) { setTimeout(cb, 10); },
});
console.log([1, 2, 3, 4, 5].map((x) => w.write(x)).join(','));
```

