What does this log?

```js
const p = new PassThrough();
p.on('readable', () => console.log('readable'));
p.on('data', (c) => console.log('data', c.toString()));
p.write('q');
p.end();
```

What does this log? Type the exact output.

```js
const e = Buffer.from('€'); // 3 bytes
const d = new StringDecoder('utf8');
console.log(JSON.stringify(d.write(e.subarray(0, 2))) + d.write(e.subarray(2)));
```

In what order are these lines logged? Note that `write` completes asynchronously.

```js
const t = new Transform({
  transform(c, e, cb) { console.log('transform', String(c)); cb(null, c); },
  flush(cb) { console.log('flush'); cb(); },
});
const w = new Writable({
  write(c, e, cb) { console.log('write', String(c)); setTimeout(cb, 5); },
  final(cb) { console.log('final'); cb(); },
});
await pipeline(Readable.from(['a', 'b']), t, w);
```
